Infrared temperatures, emissivity, reflections and source size (@th-infrared: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/Radiance-Temperature-Calibrations-NIST.lingua#r_1ZZFTRWTTE4RBKGANZJMEYQ0WE", #source "../sources/Radiative-Transfer-MIT-2-58J.lingua#r_0SGHEYZJFKN0ZNS3AYJ39XPT86", #source "../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/SI-Realizations.lingua#r_240WHEHDVW9TR241AXP6T4STM0", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/models/Observation-and-identifiability.lingua#r_5J7K2N4XB97BQSJBCXCMCJVC5W") { r_31ERZY2WADAKFR6S1X10XFG43Y
**Read:** [Radiance temperature calibrations — NIST SP 250-43](../sources/Radiance-Temperature-Calibrations-NIST.lingua#r_1ZZFTRWTTE4RBKGANZJMEYQ0WE), the complete calibration report and current laboratory context; [Radiative Transfer — MIT 2.58J](../sources/Radiative-Transfer-MIT-2-58J.lingua#r_0SGHEYZJFKN0ZNS3AYJ39XPT86), radiometric quantities and material properties; [Practical realizations of SI units — BIPM consultative committees](../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/SI-Realizations.lingua#r_240WHEHDVW9TR241AXP6T4STM0), temperature realization and calibration chains.

An infrared instrument measures radiation in a spectral and spatial response band. Converting its signal to surface temperature requires a model of emissivity, reflected surroundings, intervening optics or atmosphere, calibration and source size. A bright region can reflect a warm object rather than have the inferred local temperature.

Read the full radiance-temperature calibration method, then compare its blackbody realization with the actual surface and viewing conditions. Distinguish a calibration uncertainty from uncertainty introduced by unknown emissivity, roughness, angle, focus or motion. A nominal emissivity setting does not establish the surface's spectral response.

Compare contact and radiation measurements with their respective perturbations and response times. Design a change of viewpoint or surroundings that can discriminate reflection from a temperature change. Preserve raw radiance/count data when available, instrument settings and the model used to infer temperature; a colour image alone is a weak thermal record.

**Continue:** [What do the observations actually determine?](../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/models/Observation-and-identifiability.lingua#r_5J7K2N4XB97BQSJBCXCMCJVC5W).

